    "blue",
    "geralt",
    "he",
    "karvex",
    "red",
    "unknown",
    "violet",
    "white",
    "zephyr"
  ],
  "scene_id": "scene.Chapter_46_the_ledger_born",
  "segment_index": 0,
  "segment_count": 387,
  "segment_hash": "26da3ae3e7d8",
  "block_title": "scene.Chapter_46_the_ledger_born",
  "beats": [
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Book 9"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "CHAPTER 46: THE LEDGER-BORN"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 1: EIGHT YEARS OF PEACE"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The world healed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not completely—some scars never fade—but enough."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Eight years."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Eight years of planting and harvest, of mending walls and raising children who had never heard the scream of a plasma turret."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Eight years of trade caravans winding between Ironspire and the Sundrift Spire-town, of festivals under the twin suns, of quiet nights where the only watch kept was for wolves, not war-constructs."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt walked the length of the continent in those years, but always returned to one place."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The valley was green now."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The stream ran clear."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The hut they’d built together still stood, though he’d added a stone porch, a chimney, shelves for the trinkets people left for her—carved falcons, polished stones, dried flowers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Every week, without fail, he placed fresh blueflowers at the base of the stone marker."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The scarf on the banner was little more than threads now, the bloodstain a pale ghost in the weave."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He did not age."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The dragon armor slept against his skin, a dormant potential."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The wings, when he summoned them, were strong, responsive—but he rarely needed them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "There was no war to fly toward."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Oreck had left after the fifth year, striding east with a nod and a promise to return if ever called."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He never did."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The veterans had scattered—some to Ironspire’s guard, some to farm, some to wander."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Life moved on."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Ironspire was a city now."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Walls three times as high, towers, forges that rang from dawn till dusk."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Population: over eight hundred."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A marketplace, a school, a temple to no god in particular—just a quiet space for remembrance."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Sundrift Spire-town gleamed at the base of the Star Needle, its people a blend of engineers and mystics, drawn by the spire’s soft, steady glow."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They traded with Ironspire, shared knowledge, built a future."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And Falcon Ridge… remained empty."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A place of pilgrimage for scholars who came to study Mika’s archives, to sit in the silence where the First Tongue had been transcribed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt was its only permanent resident."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The keeper of the quiet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No Anunnaki signals had been detected in eight years."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No corruption blooms."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No temporal rifts."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The network held."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The land, though scarred, was clean."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Peace."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It felt like a held breath."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 2: THE ARRIVAL"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The stranger came at noon on a day without clouds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He walked out of the eastern badlands as though he’d always been there, his approach not seen until he was already at Ironspire’s outer gate."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Tall—seven feet if an inch—encased in armor the color of cooled magma, heat-scarred and pitted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His helm was a split-visor design, the slit glowing with a dull, ember-red light."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No insignia, no banner."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Just a heavy, weighted chain wrapped around his torso and left arm, each link engraved with a name in a script that hurt the eyes to look at."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The gate guards challenged him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He stopped, his stillness unnatural—no shift of weight, no breath misting in the cool air."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "he",
      "text": "“Where is Geralt?”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“State your business,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the captain said, hand on her sword."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“I am Karvex. The Ledger-Born. I have come to collect a debt.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“What debt?”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“The debt of unfinished stories. Unpaid balances from the war. Gods may die. Debts do not.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He wasn’t evil."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "There was no malice in his tone, no rage in his posture."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was procedural."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "An enforcer."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A cosmic bailiff."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Geralt isn’t here,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the captain said. “Leave.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex’s helm tilted slightly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Then you will produce him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Or I will begin foreclosure proceedings on this settlement.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Foreclosure?”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Destruction. Until he appears. The contract permits it.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He took one step forward."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The ground didn’t shake."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The air didn’t crackle."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "But the certainty in that step was more terrifying than any roar."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Sound the alarm,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the captain whispered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 3: THE IMPOSSIBLE FIGHT"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt felt the disturbance through the network’s echo—a pressure, a wrongness."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was at Falcon Ridge, tending the little garden Mika had started."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He straightened, his wings unfolding in a single, sharp motion."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He didn’t run."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He leapt from the ridge, caught the air, and glided toward Ironspire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He arrived as the first building fell."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex wasn’t raging."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was working."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Methodical."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Efficient."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His chain uncoiled, striking a watchtower."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The tower didn’t explode—it unmade, collapsing into dust and disconnected stones as though its history had been revoked."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No fire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No smoke."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Just erasure."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt landed between Karvex and the next building—a granary."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Stop.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex paused."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The red slit in his helm regarded Geralt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Geralt of the Dragon."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Debt-holder."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "You have answered the summons.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“I don’t owe you anything.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“The contract says otherwise. You left stories open. Lives unresolved. The ledger must be balanced.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“What ledger?”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“The Ledger of Finalities. I am its hand.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He took a step forward. “You will submit to judgment. Or I will collect from these assets.” He gestured toward Ironspire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt tried reason."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Tried diplomacy."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Tried explaining the war, the sacrifices, the peace earned."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex listened."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then said: “Irrelevant."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Contract is absolute."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Do you submit?”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“No.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Then we proceed to collection.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt summoned the dragon armor fully."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Plates snapped into place."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Wings flared."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He launched himself at Karvex."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The fight was short."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And hopeless."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt’s enhanced strength?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex absorbed the blow, the chain wrapping around Geralt’s fist, squeezing until the armor cracked."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Wing-assisted glide?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex’s chain lashed out, tangling a wing, yanking Geralt from the air."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Energy staff blast?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex didn’t dodge."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The blast hit his chest—and fizzled, as though the energy had been “repossessed.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex wasn’t faster."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Wasn’t stronger in the raw sense."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was certain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Every move Geralt made, Karvex had already accounted for in the contract’s fine print."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Karvex",
      "text": "“You have three moves left,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt panted, blood dripping from a gash on his brow."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His left wing was bent."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Armor was spiderwebbed with cracks."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He tried a desperate lunge, aiming for the helm’s slit."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex caught his wrist."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Move two.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He threw Geralt through the wall of the granary."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Stones shattered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt lay in the dust, struggling to rise."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex stood over him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Move three."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Final Notice issued."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Execution strike in three."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Two.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt looked up into that red slit."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He saw no hatred."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No pleasure."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Just procedure."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“One.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The chain rose, glowing with a cold, legal light."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It wasn’t meant to kill."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was meant to settle the account."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 4: THE SALVATION—COLORS BLUR"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Something moved—too fast to see."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A blur of cobalt and sea-foam."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt was yanked from the ground an instant before the chain struck."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The cobbles where he’d lain erupted into geometric dust."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The chain, mid-recoil, was caught."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Tangled in suddenly-living vines that burst from the earth, wrapping the links, pulling Karvex off-balance."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Yellow-white."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A streak of cutting wind, sharp as a razor."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It hit Karvex’s helm with a sound like a bell cracking."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The ember-glow flickered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Fire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not wild."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Precise."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A lance of white-hot flame that pierced Karvex’s shoulder joint, melting armor, scoring the material beneath."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex staggered—the first time he’d shown anything resembling pain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt gasped, bleeding, held upright by… nothing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The air itself supported him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He blinked, vision swimming."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Five figures stood between him and Karvex."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They weren’t standing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were arranged."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "As though they’d always been there, and the world had just now noticed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And at the center, Violet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They didn’t speak."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They didn’t look at Geralt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They faced Karvex, and reality bent around them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 5: THE FIVE STRIKE"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex straightened, his helm tilting."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“New variables."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not in the contract.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet raised a hand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The assault wasn’t an attack."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was a revision."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red didn’t throw fire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She became it—a swirling vortex of flame that didn’t burn, but unmade heat signatures, dissolving Karvex’s thermal targeting."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue didn’t summon water."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She was pressure—a crushing, deep-ocean force that compressed the air around Karvex, slowing his movements to a crawl."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green didn’t move the earth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was stability—the ground beneath Karvex’s feet rejecting him, stone flowing like liquid to encase his ankles."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White didn’t cut with air."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She was absence—the vacuum around Karvex’s helm, starving his systems of oxygen, of sound, of data."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And Violet… Violet didn’t strike."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She rewrote."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Where her gaze fell, Karvex’s contractual certainty frayed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The chain’s glow dimmed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His movements stuttered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex fought back."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His chain lashed, but it moved through them—they were elemental, intangible when they chose to be."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He tried to invoke a clause, to declare their intervention a breach, but the words dissolved in the aether around Violet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was not being defeated."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was being overruled."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "For the first time, his flat voice held something—not fear, but confusion."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“This… is not permitted.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet spoke a single word."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It wasn’t in any language Geralt knew."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was the sound of a law being repealed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Karvex’s chain went slack."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The light in his helm guttered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He didn’t collapse—he deconstructed, his armor peeling away like pages from a ledger, dissolving into dust and faint, echoing numerals."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His last words hung in the air, already fading: “Contract… suspended."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not… terminated."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The debt… remains.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then he was gone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 6: THE REVELATION"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Silence."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The five figures turned."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "For the first time, Geralt saw them clearly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red—a woman with hair like living flame, eyes like coals, skin traced with ember-lines."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue—calm, fluid, her form subtly shifting like deep water."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green—solid, grounded, moss and stone woven into his being."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White—ethereal, barely there, a whisper given shape."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet—the most defined, the most present."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A woman with eyes that held entire constellations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They approached."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt tried to stand, but his legs buckled."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet caught him, her touch cool and steady."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "One by one, they knelt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red first, placing a fist over her heart."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue, bowing her head."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green, a hand pressed to the earth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White, a slight, respectful incline."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet last, meeting Geralt’s gaze as she knelt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Violet",
      "text": "“Mika,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then, each in turn:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt’s breath caught."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He understood."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "These were not the Five he’d rescued from Xal’Zirith."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not anymore."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were what they had become in eight years of transformation—elemental avatars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And they had chosen a name."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not their own."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Hers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ADDENDUM: THE WEIGHT OF A WORD"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt stared at them, the echoes of their voices hanging in the air."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Five syllables."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Five declarations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "One name."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They had never spoken before."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not in the slave encmp, not in the aftermath of the 250 erased, not in the last moments on heaven before death took them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Their silence had been part of their nature—elemental forces didn't need words."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "But they had chosen this word."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "This name."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet’s voice had been the first—layered, harmonic, as if five voices spoke in unison, yet distinctly hers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then each in turn: Red’s voice like embers settling in a hearth; Blue’s a clear, deep well; Green’s the rumble of stone on stone; White’s the whisper through pines."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They didn’t just say it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They testified."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt’s understanding shifted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It wasn’t that they had learned to speak."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was that they had found something worth breaking silence for."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "he",
      "text": "“You… took her name,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Violet",
      "text": "“We carry it,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red stepped forward, her ember-eyes fixed on Geralt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“We chose it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Not because we forgot our own."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "But because we remembered what she was."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "What she taught by existing.” Her voice crackled, not with heat, with emotion."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“She was the first to see us as more than weapons."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "More than casualties."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She was our commander."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Our North Star.. and we are and always be your 5 loyal followers, of course we understand who she was\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green placed his hand flat on the earth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“When we were unmade, she held the line."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "When we were lost, she sent you to find us."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her will was the anchor.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue’s form shimmered like a calm sea at dawn."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“We are five rivers, but we flow to one sea."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her name is the ocean.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White simply nodded, her form barely substantial."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“She is the silence between our words."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The breath before speech.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet looked at Geralt, and for a moment, he saw not a cosmic entity, but the young warrior she had been—the one Mika had trained, had trusted, had grieved."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“We speak now because we have something to say."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are the Five Mikas."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are her lesson given form: that protection is not control."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "That power is not domination."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "That legacy is not a monument—it is a living thing.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She placed her hand over her heart, where a human heart would beat."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“We say her name to remind the world."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "To remind you."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "To remind ourselves."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are not just elements."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are her students."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And we are here.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The silence that followed was different from before."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It wasn’t empty."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was full of the echo of that name, now woven into the fabric of their being."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt felt the tears then, hot and unashamed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They weren’t just tears of grief, or gratitude."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were tears of recognition."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika hadn’t just left a book."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She hadn’t just left a memory."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She had left a vocabulary of hope, spoken in the voices of the elements themselves."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“She would be proud,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "he managed, his voice thick."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red smiled, a small, fierce thing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“We know.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And in that moment, Geralt understood the true transformation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They hadn’t just gained power."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They had gained a voice."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And their first word, their chosen word, was the name of the woman who taught them that even the most broken stories could have a beautiful sequel."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 7: THE GRATITUDE"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They helped him to his feet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Around them, Ironspire’s people stared, silent, awed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Geralt",
      "text": "“You saved me,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Red",
      "text": "“You saved us first,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Blue",
      "text": "“We felt your need,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“We are connected,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green rumbled. “To this land. To you. To her memory.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "White",
      "text": "“We do not stay,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet placed a hand on Geralt’s chest, over the dormant dragon armor."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“You are not alone, Geralt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Even when you feel solitude."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are here."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "In the fire, the water, the stone, the air, the aether."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "We are the Five Mikas."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And we remember.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She leaned forward, pressed her forehead to his—a gesture of deep respect, of kinship."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Tell her we said thank you.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then, one by one, they faded."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Red into a shower of sparks."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Blue into rising mist."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Green into sinking stone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "White into a sigh of wind."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Violet last, into a shimmer of violet light that hung in the air for a moment before dissolving."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt stood alone in the courtyard, the broken chain-links of Karvex crumbling to dust at his feet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 8: ZEPHYR RETURNS"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Three days later, at Mika’s grave, Zephyr appeared."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He didn’t arrive."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was simply there, sitting cross-legged beside the stone marker, tracing the letters of her name with one finger."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Geralt",
      "text": "“They came,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“They did.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“You knew they would.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“I knew what they were becoming. I didn’t know what they would choose to call themselves.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr smiled, a rare, genuine expression. “Mika. Of course.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“They’re legends now.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“They always were. Now the world will know it.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr stood. “They’ll appear in stories. The Five Mikas who come when heroes are at their end. Who arrive not with thunder, but with elements. Teachers. Protectors. Her name will outlive stone.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt looked at the grave, then at the valley, then at the distant spire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“She wanted to be a teacher."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Now she’s five of them.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Zephyr",
      "text": "“Her legacy is secure,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "“Yes. Karvex was a warning. The debts of the past are coming due. The universe keeps books. And you still have pages left to write.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt took a long, slow breath."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The peace was over."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The next war wasn’t against empires or corruptions."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was against fate itself."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Against ledgers and contracts and the cosmic debt he didn’t know he owed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "he",
      "text": "“I’m ready,”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr nodded."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "“Then let us go and finish what you started."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Let us make you the guardian the next age will need.”"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He offered his hand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt took it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The sun set over Falcon Ridge, painting the sky in the colors of the Five Mikas: red, blue, green, white, violet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And somewhere between the elements, between memory and legend, five pairs of eyes watched Geralt walk away, ready to become what came next."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "END OF CHAPTER 46"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "line": 1,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Book 9"
    },
    {
      "line": 3,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "CHAPTER 46: THE LEDGER-BORN"
    },
    {
      "line": 5,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 1: EIGHT YEARS OF PEACE"
    },
    {
      "line": 7,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The world healed."
    },
    {
      "line": 8,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not completely—some scars never fade—but enough."
    },
    {
      "line": 10,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Eight years."
    },
    {
      "line": 12,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Eight years of planting and harvest, of mending walls and raising children who had never heard the scream of a plasma turret."
    },
    {
      "line": 13,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Eight years of trade caravans winding between Ironspire and the Sundrift Spire-town, of festivals under the twin suns, of quiet nights where the only watch kept was for wolves, not war-constructs."
    },
    {
      "line": 15,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt walked the length of the continent in those years, but always returned to one place."
    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "line": 19,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The valley was green now."
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stream ran clear."
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The hut they’d built together still stood, though he’d added a stone porch, a chimney, shelves for the trinkets people left for her—carved falcons, polished stones, dried flowers."
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Every week, without fail, he placed fresh blueflowers at the base of the stone marker."
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarf on the banner was little more than threads now, the bloodstain a pale ghost in the weave."
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He did not age."
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The dragon armor slept against his skin, a dormant potential."
    },
    {
      "line": 28,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The wings, when he summoned them, were strong, responsive—but he rarely needed them."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "There was no war to fly toward."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Oreck had left after the fifth year, striding east with a nod and a promise to return if ever called."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He never did."
    },
    {
      "line": 33,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The veterans had scattered—some to Ironspire’s guard, some to farm, some to wander."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Life moved on."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ironspire was a city now."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Walls three times as high, towers, forges that rang from dawn till dusk."
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Population: over eight hundred."
    },
    {
      "line": 39,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A marketplace, a school, a temple to no god in particular—just a quiet space for remembrance."
    },
    {
      "line": 41,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sundrift Spire-town gleamed at the base of the Star Needle, its people a blend of engineers and mystics, drawn by the spire’s soft, steady glow."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They traded with Ironspire, shared knowledge, built a future."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And Falcon Ridge… remained empty."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A place of pilgrimage for scholars who came to study Mika’s archives, to sit in the silence where the First Tongue had been transcribed."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt was its only permanent resident."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The keeper of the quiet."
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Anunnaki signals had been detected in eight years."
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No corruption blooms."
    },
    {
      "line": 51,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No temporal rifts."
    },
    {
      "line": 52,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The network held."
    },
    {
      "line": 53,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The land, though scarred, was clean."
    },
    {
      "line": 55,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Peace."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It felt like a held breath."
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 61,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 2: THE ARRIVAL"
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stranger came at noon on a day without clouds."
    },
    {
      "line": 65,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He walked out of the eastern badlands as though he’d always been there, his approach not seen until he was already at Ironspire’s outer gate."
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Tall—seven feet if an inch—encased in armor the color of cooled magma, heat-scarred and pitted."
    },
    {
      "line": 67,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His helm was a split-visor design, the slit glowing with a dull, ember-red light."
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No insignia, no banner."
    },
    {
      "line": 69,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just a heavy, weighted chain wrapped around his torso and left arm, each link engraved with a name in a script that hurt the eyes to look at."
    },
    {
      "line": 71,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The gate guards challenged him."
    },
    {
      "line": 72,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He stopped, his stillness unnatural—no shift of weight, no breath misting in the cool air."
    },
    {
      "line": 74,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "he",
      "text": "“Where is Geralt?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 76,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“State your business,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 77,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the captain said, hand on her sword."
    },
    {
      "line": 79,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“I am Karvex. The Ledger-Born. I have come to collect a debt.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 81,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“What debt?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 83,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“The debt of unfinished stories. Unpaid balances from the war. Gods may die. Debts do not.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 85,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He wasn’t evil."
    },
    {
      "line": 86,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "There was no malice in his tone, no rage in his posture."
    },
    {
      "line": 87,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was procedural."
    },
    {
      "line": 88,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "An enforcer."
    },
    {
      "line": 89,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A cosmic bailiff."
    },
    {
      "line": 91,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Geralt isn’t here,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 92,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the captain said. “Leave.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 94,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex’s helm tilted slightly."
    },
    {
      "line": 95,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Then you will produce him."
    },
    {
      "line": 96,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Or I will begin foreclosure proceedings on this settlement.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Foreclosure?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 100,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Destruction. Until he appears. The contract permits it.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He took one step forward."
    },
    {
      "line": 103,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The ground didn’t shake."
    },
    {
      "line": 104,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The air didn’t crackle."
    },
    {
      "line": 105,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But the certainty in that step was more terrifying than any roar."
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Sound the alarm,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the captain whispered."
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 112,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 3: THE IMPOSSIBLE FIGHT"
    },
    {
      "line": 114,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt felt the disturbance through the network’s echo—a pressure, a wrongness."
    },
    {
      "line": 115,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was at Falcon Ridge, tending the little garden Mika had started."
    },
    {
      "line": 116,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He straightened, his wings unfolding in a single, sharp motion."
    },
    {
      "line": 117,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He didn’t run."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He leapt from the ridge, caught the air, and glided toward Ironspire."
    },
    {
      "line": 120,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He arrived as the first building fell."
    },
    {
      "line": 122,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex wasn’t raging."
    },
    {
      "line": 123,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was working."
    },
    {
      "line": 124,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Methodical."
    },
    {
      "line": 125,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Efficient."
    },
    {
      "line": 126,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His chain uncoiled, striking a watchtower."
    },
    {
      "line": 127,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The tower didn’t explode—it unmade, collapsing into dust and disconnected stones as though its history had been revoked."
    },
    {
      "line": 128,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No fire."
    },
    {
      "line": 129,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No smoke."
    },
    {
      "line": 130,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just erasure."
    },
    {
      "line": 132,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt landed between Karvex and the next building—a granary."
    },
    {
      "line": 134,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Stop.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 136,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex paused."
    },
    {
      "line": 137,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The red slit in his helm regarded Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 138,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Geralt of the Dragon."
    },
    {
      "line": 139,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Debt-holder."
    },
    {
      "line": 140,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "You have answered the summons.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 142,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“I don’t owe you anything.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 144,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“The contract says otherwise. You left stories open. Lives unresolved. The ledger must be balanced.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 146,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“What ledger?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 148,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“The Ledger of Finalities. I am its hand.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 149,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He took a step forward. “You will submit to judgment. Or I will collect from these assets.” He gestured toward Ironspire."
    },
    {
      "line": 151,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt tried reason."
    },
    {
      "line": 152,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Tried diplomacy."
    },
    {
      "line": 153,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Tried explaining the war, the sacrifices, the peace earned."
    },
    {
      "line": 155,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex listened."
    },
    {
      "line": 156,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then said: “Irrelevant."
    },
    {
      "line": 157,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Contract is absolute."
    },
    {
      "line": 158,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Do you submit?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 160,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“No.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 162,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Then we proceed to collection.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 164,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt summoned the dragon armor fully."
    },
    {
      "line": 165,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Plates snapped into place."
    },
    {
      "line": 166,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wings flared."
    },
    {
      "line": 167,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He launched himself at Karvex."
    },
    {
      "line": 169,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The fight was short."
    },
    {
      "line": 170,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And hopeless."
    },
    {
      "line": 172,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt’s enhanced strength?"
    },
    {
      "line": 173,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex absorbed the blow, the chain wrapping around Geralt’s fist, squeezing until the armor cracked."
    },
    {
      "line": 175,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wing-assisted glide?"
    },
    {
      "line": 176,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex’s chain lashed out, tangling a wing, yanking Geralt from the air."
    },
    {
      "line": 178,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Energy staff blast?"
    },
    {
      "line": 179,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex didn’t dodge."
    },
    {
      "line": 180,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The blast hit his chest—and fizzled, as though the energy had been “repossessed.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 182,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex wasn’t faster."
    },
    {
      "line": 183,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wasn’t stronger in the raw sense."
    },
    {
      "line": 184,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was certain."
    },
    {
      "line": 185,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Every move Geralt made, Karvex had already accounted for in the contract’s fine print."
    },
    {
      "line": 187,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Karvex",
      "text": "“You have three moves left,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 189,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt panted, blood dripping from a gash on his brow."
    },
    {
      "line": 190,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His left wing was bent."
    },
    {
      "line": 191,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Armor was spiderwebbed with cracks."
    },
    {
      "line": 193,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He tried a desperate lunge, aiming for the helm’s slit."
    },
    {
      "line": 195,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex caught his wrist."
    },
    {
      "line": 196,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Move two.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 198,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He threw Geralt through the wall of the granary."
    },
    {
      "line": 199,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Stones shattered."
    },
    {
      "line": 200,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt lay in the dust, struggling to rise."
    },
    {
      "line": 202,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex stood over him."
    },
    {
      "line": 203,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Move three."
    },
    {
      "line": 204,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Final Notice issued."
    },
    {
      "line": 205,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Execution strike in three."
    },
    {
      "line": 206,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Two.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 208,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt looked up into that red slit."
    },
    {
      "line": 209,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He saw no hatred."
    },
    {
      "line": 210,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No pleasure."
    },
    {
      "line": 211,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just procedure."
    },
    {
      "line": 213,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“One.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 215,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chain rose, glowing with a cold, legal light."
    },
    {
      "line": 216,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It wasn’t meant to kill."
    },
    {
      "line": 217,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was meant to settle the account."
    },
    {
      "line": 219,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 221,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 4: THE SALVATION—COLORS BLUR"
    },
    {
      "line": 223,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue."
    },
    {
      "line": 225,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Something moved—too fast to see."
    },
    {
      "line": 226,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A blur of cobalt and sea-foam."
    },
    {
      "line": 227,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt was yanked from the ground an instant before the chain struck."
    },
    {
      "line": 228,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The cobbles where he’d lain erupted into geometric dust."
    },
    {
      "line": 230,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green."
    },
    {
      "line": 232,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chain, mid-recoil, was caught."
    },
    {
      "line": 233,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Tangled in suddenly-living vines that burst from the earth, wrapping the links, pulling Karvex off-balance."
    },
    {
      "line": 235,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Yellow-white."
    },
    {
      "line": 237,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A streak of cutting wind, sharp as a razor."
    },
    {
      "line": 238,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It hit Karvex’s helm with a sound like a bell cracking."
    },
    {
      "line": 239,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The ember-glow flickered."
    },
    {
      "line": 241,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red."
    },
    {
      "line": 243,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Fire."
    },
    {
      "line": 244,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not wild."
    },
    {
      "line": 245,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Precise."
    },
    {
      "line": 246,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A lance of white-hot flame that pierced Karvex’s shoulder joint, melting armor, scoring the material beneath."
    },
    {
      "line": 247,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex staggered—the first time he’d shown anything resembling pain."
    },
    {
      "line": 249,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt gasped, bleeding, held upright by… nothing."
    },
    {
      "line": 250,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The air itself supported him."
    },
    {
      "line": 251,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He blinked, vision swimming."
    },
    {
      "line": 253,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Five figures stood between him and Karvex."
    },
    {
      "line": 255,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They weren’t standing."
    },
    {
      "line": 256,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were arranged."
    },
    {
      "line": 257,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "As though they’d always been there, and the world had just now noticed."
    },
    {
      "line": 259,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red."
    },
    {
      "line": 260,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue."
    },
    {
      "line": 261,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green."
    },
    {
      "line": 262,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White."
    },
    {
      "line": 263,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And at the center, Violet."
    },
    {
      "line": 265,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They didn’t speak."
    },
    {
      "line": 266,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They didn’t look at Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 267,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They faced Karvex, and reality bent around them."
    },
    {
      "line": 269,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 271,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 5: THE FIVE STRIKE"
    },
    {
      "line": 273,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex straightened, his helm tilting."
    },
    {
      "line": 274,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“New variables."
    },
    {
      "line": 275,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not in the contract.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 277,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet raised a hand."
    },
    {
      "line": 279,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The assault wasn’t an attack."
    },
    {
      "line": 280,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was a revision."
    },
    {
      "line": 282,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red didn’t throw fire."
    },
    {
      "line": 283,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She became it—a swirling vortex of flame that didn’t burn, but unmade heat signatures, dissolving Karvex’s thermal targeting."
    },
    {
      "line": 285,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue didn’t summon water."
    },
    {
      "line": 286,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She was pressure—a crushing, deep-ocean force that compressed the air around Karvex, slowing his movements to a crawl."
    },
    {
      "line": 288,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green didn’t move the earth."
    },
    {
      "line": 289,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was stability—the ground beneath Karvex’s feet rejecting him, stone flowing like liquid to encase his ankles."
    },
    {
      "line": 291,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White didn’t cut with air."
    },
    {
      "line": 292,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She was absence—the vacuum around Karvex’s helm, starving his systems of oxygen, of sound, of data."
    },
    {
      "line": 294,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And Violet… Violet didn’t strike."
    },
    {
      "line": 295,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She rewrote."
    },
    {
      "line": 297,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Where her gaze fell, Karvex’s contractual certainty frayed."
    },
    {
      "line": 298,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chain’s glow dimmed."
    },
    {
      "line": 299,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His movements stuttered."
    },
    {
      "line": 301,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex fought back."
    },
    {
      "line": 302,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His chain lashed, but it moved through them—they were elemental, intangible when they chose to be."
    },
    {
      "line": 303,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He tried to invoke a clause, to declare their intervention a breach, but the words dissolved in the aether around Violet."
    },
    {
      "line": 305,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was not being defeated."
    },
    {
      "line": 306,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was being overruled."
    },
    {
      "line": 308,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For the first time, his flat voice held something—not fear, but confusion."
    },
    {
      "line": 309,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“This… is not permitted.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 311,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet spoke a single word."
    },
    {
      "line": 312,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It wasn’t in any language Geralt knew."
    },
    {
      "line": 313,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was the sound of a law being repealed."
    },
    {
      "line": 315,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Karvex’s chain went slack."
    },
    {
      "line": 316,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The light in his helm guttered."
    },
    {
      "line": 317,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He didn’t collapse—he deconstructed, his armor peeling away like pages from a ledger, dissolving into dust and faint, echoing numerals."
    },
    {
      "line": 319,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His last words hung in the air, already fading: “Contract… suspended."
    },
    {
      "line": 320,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not… terminated."
    },
    {
      "line": 321,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The debt… remains.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 323,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then he was gone."
    },
    {
      "line": 325,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 327,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 6: THE REVELATION"
    },
    {
      "line": 329,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Silence."
    },
    {
      "line": 331,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The five figures turned."
    },
    {
      "line": 332,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For the first time, Geralt saw them clearly."
    },
    {
      "line": 334,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red—a woman with hair like living flame, eyes like coals, skin traced with ember-lines."
    },
    {
      "line": 335,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue—calm, fluid, her form subtly shifting like deep water."
    },
    {
      "line": 336,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green—solid, grounded, moss and stone woven into his being."
    },
    {
      "line": 337,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White—ethereal, barely there, a whisper given shape."
    },
    {
      "line": 338,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet—the most defined, the most present."
    },
    {
      "line": 339,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A woman with eyes that held entire constellations."
    },
    {
      "line": 341,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They approached."
    },
    {
      "line": 342,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt tried to stand, but his legs buckled."
    },
    {
      "line": 343,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet caught him, her touch cool and steady."
    },
    {
      "line": 345,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One by one, they knelt."
    },
    {
      "line": 347,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red first, placing a fist over her heart."
    },
    {
      "line": 348,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue, bowing her head."
    },
    {
      "line": 349,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green, a hand pressed to the earth."
    },
    {
      "line": 350,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White, a slight, respectful incline."
    },
    {
      "line": 351,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet last, meeting Geralt’s gaze as she knelt."
    },
    {
      "line": 353,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Violet",
      "text": "“Mika,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 355,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then, each in turn:"
    },
    {
      "line": 357,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 358,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 359,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 360,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Mika.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 362,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt’s breath caught."
    },
    {
      "line": 363,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He understood."
    },
    {
      "line": 365,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "These were not the Five he’d rescued from Xal’Zirith."
    },
    {
      "line": 366,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not anymore."
    },
    {
      "line": 367,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were what they had become in eight years of transformation—elemental avatars."
    },
    {
      "line": 368,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And they had chosen a name."
    },
    {
      "line": 369,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not their own."
    },
    {
      "line": 370,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hers."
    },
    {
      "line": 372,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ADDENDUM: THE WEIGHT OF A WORD"
    },
    {
      "line": 374,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt stared at them, the echoes of their voices hanging in the air."
    },
    {
      "line": 375,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Five syllables."
    },
    {
      "line": 376,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Five declarations."
    },
    {
      "line": 377,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One name."
    },
    {
      "line": 379,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika."
    },
    {
      "line": 381,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They had never spoken before."
    },
    {
      "line": 382,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not in the slave encmp, not in the aftermath of the 250 erased, not in the last moments on heaven before death took them."
    },
    {
      "line": 383,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Their silence had been part of their nature—elemental forces didn't need words."
    },
    {
      "line": 384,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were."
    },
    {
      "line": 386,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But they had chosen this word."
    },
    {
      "line": 387,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This name."
    },
    {
      "line": 389,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet’s voice had been the first—layered, harmonic, as if five voices spoke in unison, yet distinctly hers."
    },
    {
      "line": 390,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then each in turn: Red’s voice like embers settling in a hearth; Blue’s a clear, deep well; Green’s the rumble of stone on stone; White’s the whisper through pines."
    },
    {
      "line": 392,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They didn’t just say it."
    },
    {
      "line": 393,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They testified."
    },
    {
      "line": 395,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt’s understanding shifted."
    },
    {
      "line": 396,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It wasn’t that they had learned to speak."
    },
    {
      "line": 397,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was that they had found something worth breaking silence for."
    },
    {
      "line": 399,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "he",
      "text": "“You… took her name,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 401,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Violet",
      "text": "“We carry it,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 403,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red stepped forward, her ember-eyes fixed on Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 404,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We chose it."
    },
    {
      "line": 405,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not because we forgot our own."
    },
    {
      "line": 406,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But because we remembered what she was."
    },
    {
      "line": 407,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "What she taught by existing.” Her voice crackled, not with heat, with emotion."
    },
    {
      "line": 408,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“She was the first to see us as more than weapons."
    },
    {
      "line": 409,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "More than casualties."
    },
    {
      "line": 410,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She was our commander."
    },
    {
      "line": 411,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Our North Star.. and we are and always be your 5 loyal followers, of course we understand who she was\""
    },
    {
      "line": 413,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green placed his hand flat on the earth."
    },
    {
      "line": 414,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“When we were unmade, she held the line."
    },
    {
      "line": 415,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "When we were lost, she sent you to find us."
    },
    {
      "line": 416,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her will was the anchor.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 418,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue’s form shimmered like a calm sea at dawn."
    },
    {
      "line": 419,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We are five rivers, but we flow to one sea."
    },
    {
      "line": 420,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her name is the ocean.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 422,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White simply nodded, her form barely substantial."
    },
    {
      "line": 423,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“She is the silence between our words."
    },
    {
      "line": 424,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The breath before speech.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 426,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet looked at Geralt, and for a moment, he saw not a cosmic entity, but the young warrior she had been—the one Mika had trained, had trusted, had grieved."
    },
    {
      "line": 427,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We speak now because we have something to say."
    },
    {
      "line": 428,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are the Five Mikas."
    },
    {
      "line": 429,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are her lesson given form: that protection is not control."
    },
    {
      "line": 430,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "That power is not domination."
    },
    {
      "line": 431,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "That legacy is not a monument—it is a living thing.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 433,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She placed her hand over her heart, where a human heart would beat."
    },
    {
      "line": 434,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We say her name to remind the world."
    },
    {
      "line": 435,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To remind you."
    },
    {
      "line": 436,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To remind ourselves."
    },
    {
      "line": 437,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are not just elements."
    },
    {
      "line": 438,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are her students."
    },
    {
      "line": 439,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And we are here.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 441,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The silence that followed was different from before."
    },
    {
      "line": 442,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It wasn’t empty."
    },
    {
      "line": 443,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was full of the echo of that name, now woven into the fabric of their being."
    },
    {
      "line": 445,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt felt the tears then, hot and unashamed."
    },
    {
      "line": 446,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They weren’t just tears of grief, or gratitude."
    },
    {
      "line": 447,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were tears of recognition."
    },
    {
      "line": 448,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika hadn’t just left a book."
    },
    {
      "line": 449,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She hadn’t just left a memory."
    },
    {
      "line": 450,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She had left a vocabulary of hope, spoken in the voices of the elements themselves."
    },
    {
      "line": 452,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“She would be proud,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 453,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "he managed, his voice thick."
    },
    {
      "line": 455,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red smiled, a small, fierce thing."
    },
    {
      "line": 456,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We know.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 458,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And in that moment, Geralt understood the true transformation."
    },
    {
      "line": 459,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They hadn’t just gained power."
    },
    {
      "line": 460,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They had gained a voice."
    },
    {
      "line": 461,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And their first word, their chosen word, was the name of the woman who taught them that even the most broken stories could have a beautiful sequel."
    },
    {
      "line": 463,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 7: THE GRATITUDE"
    },
    {
      "line": 465,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They helped him to his feet."
    },
    {
      "line": 466,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Around them, Ironspire’s people stared, silent, awed."
    },
    {
      "line": 468,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "text": "“You saved me,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 470,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Red",
      "text": "“You saved us first,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 472,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Blue",
      "text": "“We felt your need,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 474,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“We are connected,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 475,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green rumbled. “To this land. To you. To her memory.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 477,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "White",
      "text": "“We do not stay,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 479,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet placed a hand on Geralt’s chest, over the dormant dragon armor."
    },
    {
      "line": 480,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“You are not alone, Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 481,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Even when you feel solitude."
    },
    {
      "line": 482,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are here."
    },
    {
      "line": 483,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "In the fire, the water, the stone, the air, the aether."
    },
    {
      "line": 484,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We are the Five Mikas."
    },
    {
      "line": 485,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And we remember.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 487,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She leaned forward, pressed her forehead to his—a gesture of deep respect, of kinship."
    },
    {
      "line": 488,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Tell her we said thank you.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 490,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then, one by one, they faded."
    },
    {
      "line": 492,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Red into a shower of sparks."
    },
    {
      "line": 493,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Blue into rising mist."
    },
    {
      "line": 494,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Green into sinking stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 495,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "White into a sigh of wind."
    },
    {
      "line": 496,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Violet last, into a shimmer of violet light that hung in the air for a moment before dissolving."
    },
    {
      "line": 498,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt stood alone in the courtyard, the broken chain-links of Karvex crumbling to dust at his feet."
    },
    {
      "line": 500,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 502,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 8: ZEPHYR RETURNS"
    },
    {
      "line": 504,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Three days later, at Mika’s grave, Zephyr appeared."
    },
    {
      "line": 506,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He didn’t arrive."
    },
    {
      "line": 507,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was simply there, sitting cross-legged beside the stone marker, tracing the letters of her name with one finger."
    },
    {
      "line": 509,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "text": "“They came,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 511,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“They did.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 513,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“You knew they would.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 515,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“I knew what they were becoming. I didn’t know what they would choose to call themselves.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 516,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr smiled, a rare, genuine expression. “Mika. Of course.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 518,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“They’re legends now.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 520,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“They always were. Now the world will know it.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 521,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr stood. “They’ll appear in stories. The Five Mikas who come when heroes are at their end. Who arrive not with thunder, but with elements. Teachers. Protectors. Her name will outlive stone.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 523,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt looked at the grave, then at the valley, then at the distant spire."
    },
    {
      "line": 524,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“She wanted to be a teacher."
    },
    {
      "line": 525,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Now she’s five of them.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 527,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Zephyr",
      "text": "“Her legacy is secure,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 529,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "“Yes. Karvex was a warning. The debts of the past are coming due. The universe keeps books. And you still have pages left to write.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 531,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt took a long, slow breath."
    },
    {
      "line": 532,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The peace was over."
    },
    {
      "line": 533,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The next war wasn’t against empires or corruptions."
    },
    {
      "line": 534,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was against fate itself."
    },
    {
      "line": 535,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Against ledgers and contracts and the cosmic debt he didn’t know he owed."
    },
    {
      "line": 537,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "he",
      "text": "“I’m ready,”"
    },
    {
      "line": 539,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr nodded."
    },
    {
      "line": 540,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Then let us go and finish what you started."
    },
    {
      "line": 541,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Let us make you the guardian the next age will need.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 543,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He offered his hand."
    },
    {
      "line": 545,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt took it."
    },
    {
      "line": 547,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The sun set over Falcon Ridge, painting the sky in the colors of the Five Mikas: red, blue, green, white, violet."
    },
    {
      "line": 549,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And somewhere between the elements, between memory and legend, five pairs of eyes watched Geralt walk away, ready to become what came next."
    },
    {
      "line": 551,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 553,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "END OF CHAPTER 46"
    }
  ]
}